              "bbox": [
                0.115,
                0.888,
                0.332,
                0.905
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 13.16: Water pollution"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.39,
            0.709,
            0.883,
            0.746
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "better waste management and sustainable farming practices."
            }
          ],
          "continues_prev": true
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.39,
            0.747,
            0.884,
            0.897
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We have seen above that all the Earth system, such as hydrosphere, biosphere, atmosphere and geosphere are connected—so damage to one can affect the others. Protecting the climate means cutting down on greenhouse gases by using renewable energy like solar and wind, improving energy use, and choosing environmentally friendly ways to travel. At the same time, preserving"
            }
